{
  "requirement": "TBV automatically redacts recognized credentials in source excerpts delivered\nby its inspection tools and in node text supplied to its agent requests.\nThe built-in rules replace recognized secret regions with redaction markers\nwhile preserving line breaks. SDK-supplied outline languages use the same redacted\nregions, so changing only a recognized credential does not change its\nstructural fingerprint.\n\nLoaded source snapshots retain the original text for selection and spans;\nredaction applies when preparing model-visible text and structural hashes.\nFilesystem evidence storage preserves the supplied record. Applications supply\ntheir own answer values and remain responsible for what those answers contain.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.sources.redaction`. I found no adequacy gap.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n1. **Redaction in source excerpts from inspection tools.**\n   - `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging]` runs both `search_text` and `search_structure` over a file holding a GitHub token and a multi-line RSA private key.\n   - It asserts the exact excerpt: both markers appear, surrounding code is unchanged, and the line count matches the original.\n   - It asserts the raw token and every key-body line are absent from the serialized output.\n   - It asserts the dependency fingerprint is the unredacted snapshot's.\n   - It asserts the file on disk is unchanged.\n   - The other inspection tools (`list_sources`, `outline_source`) return identities, selectors and kinds, not source text.\n   - `read_node` is the tool that delivers node text, and it is covered under item 2.\n\n2. **Redaction of node text in agent requests.**\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[queued_contents_and_graph_read_tools_redact_credentials_before_delivery]` drives both the queued `contents_of_current_node` path and the `read_node` tool.\n   - It checks that every request's serialized chat history lacks the secret and contains the marker.\n   - It checks that the recorded dependency fingerprint and the graph contents stay the original text.\n\n3. **Markers replace secret regions while line breaks are preserved.**\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[private_keys_are_redacted_from_header_through_body_keeping_lines]` checks the exact output and line counts, for both a bare key and a key inside Rust code.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[regions_extend_both_ways_keep_crlf_and_scan_past_a_mebibyte]` checks CRLF preservation, region extension over adjacent entropy-like tokens, and a scan past 1 MiB.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[tokens_in_code_are_redacted_without_adjacent_code]` checks that adjacent code is untouched.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[slices_concatenate_to_the_redacted_whole]` checks that redacted slices concatenate to the redacted whole.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[heuristic_findings_alone_are_not_redacted]` checks the negative case: heuristic-only findings are not redacted.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[configuration_keys_do_not_add_sdk_specific_secret_rules]` checks that built-in rules only, with no SDK-specific key rules, are applied.\n\n4. **Outline languages use the same redacted regions, so changing only a credential does not change the structural fingerprint.**\n   - `outline/redaction_tests.rs#fn[hashes_do_not_depend_on_credential_values]` covers Rust, Markdown and plain text. It also asserts that a change outside the redacted region does change the hash.\n   - `outline/redaction_tests.rs#fn[redaction_never_changes_an_outline]` covers YAML, Rust, TOML, Markdown and text, including the YAML case where parsing the redacted text would change the outline.\n   - `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[formatted_contents_redact_credentials_while_retaining_raw_text_and_spans]` shows that replacing only the token leaves `OutlineContent::fingerprint` equal.\n\n5. **Snapshots retain the original text for selection and spans, and redaction applies only to model-visible text and hashes.** The same `tests/outline_content.rs` test asserts `text()` equals the original and that `format()` is redacted. The selected sub-node's `text()` still contains the token while its `format()` does not.\n\n6. **Filesystem evidence storage preserves the supplied record.** `tests/storage.rs#fn[storage_preserves_completed_answers_containing_credential_shaped_text]` round-trips an answer containing a token-shaped string. It asserts equality on load and that the stored bytes contain the token.\n\n7. **Applications supply their own answers and remain responsible for their contents.** This states a responsibility and imposes no behavior to test, apart from the storage preservation in item 6.\n\n**Provider-based `SourceSession` tools**\n\nI looked at the provider-based `SourceSession` tools in `agent/sources.rs`. The `ToolFactory` for them is only reachable through a `#[cfg(test)]` wrapper in `agent.rs`, and no redaction test targets them. They are not the project inspection path, which is the one `{impl}`-marked for this requirement. I did not count them as an obligation in scope.\n\nNo unresolved ambiguities remain, and no {fixme} acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "bd6b2738ddefb950bba56fda9c12fc5c2ff07ea9457dd6ccdaff4a64d36d0017",
